==============================================================================
PART 3 -- the two FORCED-PASS lemmas, and how much of round 40's census they eat
==============================================================================
  (PER-A)  If diam = rad+1 and w is not a centre, then ecc(w) = diam.
           Proof: ecc(w) >= rad+1 = diam, and ecc(w) <= diam always.  QED
  (PER-B)  If ecc(w) = 2*rad, then ecc(w) = diam.
           Proof: for any centre c and any x,y: d(x,y) <= d(x,c)+d(c,y) <= 2*rad, so
           diam <= 2*rad; and ecc(w) <= diam.  Hence 2*rad <= diam <= 2*rad.  QED
  (PER-C)  So (RXM-PERI) can only FAIL at an instance with diam >= rad+2 AND ecc(w) < 2*rad.
           Call such an instance OPEN; every other instance is a FORCED PASS and is evidence
           for nothing.
  PREDICTION REGISTERED BEFORE THE RUN: all 1297 census instances are FORCED PASSES,
  i.e. the count of OPEN instances is 0 and round 40's 1297/1297 tested nothing.
  hosts rebuilt: 417 (skipped 3 as too big)
  hosts with diam >= rad+2 at all: 190
  condition-3 instances: 1297
    FORCED by (PER-A) diam = rad+1 : 414
    FORCED by (PER-B) ecc(w) = 2rad: 883
    forced by BOTH                 : 0
    OPEN (the only ones that test the conjecture): 0
    violations among the OPEN ones: 0
  >> PREDICTION HELD.  Round 40's 1297/1297 is a union of two one-line lemmas;
     it contains ZERO instances of the only regime in which (RXM-PERI) has content.

